{:edb/db-before-t 1561 :edb/db-after-t 1562 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534874 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:45:12.939Z" 13194139534874 true] [17592186124115 1100 "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ given that $f(x,y) = 3x\\ln y + 2ye^x$." 13194139534874 false] [17592186124115 1100 "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ given that $f(x,y) = 3x\\ln y + 2ye^x.$" 13194139534874 true] [17592186124115 1145 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y$, treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y} &= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\ln y + 2ye^{x}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\ln y) + \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2ye^{x}) \\\\\n&= 3x \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln y) + 2e^{x} \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\\n&= 3x \\cdot \\frac{1}{y} + 2e^{x} \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3x}{y} + 2e^{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534874 false] [17592186124115 1145 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)+2{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{y}+2{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534874 true] [17592186124119 1100 "Given that $f(x,y) = y^2\\ln{x}$, express $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ as the limit of a difference quotient." 13194139534874 false] [17592186124119 1100 "Given that $f(x,y) = y^2\\ln{x},$ express $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ as the limit of a difference quotient." 13194139534874 true] [17592186124119 1145 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\left(\\dfrac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right)\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nf(x) = y^2 \\ln{x}\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\nf(x+h,y) = y^2\\ln(x+h)\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0}\\left(\\dfrac{y^2\\ln(x+h) -y^2\\ln{x}}{h}\\right)\n$$" 13194139534874 false] [17592186124119 1145 "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\left(\\dfrac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}\\right).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x) = y^2 \\ln{x},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y) = y^2\\ln(x+h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} = \\lim_{h \\to 0}\\left( \\dfrac{y^2\\ln(x+h) -y^2\\ln{x} }{h}\\right).\n$$" 13194139534874 true] [17592186124120 1100 "For the function $f(x,y) = x^2y^2+\\sin{x}\\cos{y}$, evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi)$." 13194139534874 false] [17592186124120 1100 "For the function $f(x,y) = x^2y^2+\\sin{x}\\cos{y},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi).$" 13194139534874 true] [17592186124120 1145 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x$, treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}y^{2} + \\sin x\\cos y) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}y^{2}) + \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin x\\cos y) \\\\\n&= y^{2} \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}) + \\cos y \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin x) \\\\\n&= y^{2} \\cdot (2x) + \\cos y \\cdot (\\cos x) \\\\\n&= 2xy^{2} + \\cos x\\cos y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\mid _{(π, 2π)} &= 2 \\cdot π \\cdot (2π)^{2} + \\cos π \\cdot \\cos 2π \\\\\n&= 2π \\cdot 4π^{2} + (-1) \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 8π^{3} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534874 false] [17592186124120 1145 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi,2\\pi)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,2\\pi )} & =2\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\pi )^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 4{\\pi }^{2}+(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8{\\pi }^{3}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534874 true] [17592186124560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316634 13194139534874 true] [17592186124560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316641 13194139534874 true] [17592186124560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316648 13194139534874 true] [17592186124560 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316655 13194139534874 true] [17592186124564 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316564 13194139534874 true] [17592186124564 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316571 13194139534874 true] [17592186124564 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316585 13194139534874 true] [17592186124564 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316592 13194139534874 true] [17592186124564 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316599 13194139534874 true] [17592186124565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316578 13194139534874 true] [17592186124565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316606 13194139534874 true] [17592186124565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316613 13194139534874 true] [17592186124565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316620 13194139534874 true] [17592186124565 1020 #edb/ref 17592186316627 13194139534874 true] [17592186124817 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534874 true] [17592186124817 1